% ADJ52 case-6 — patient observations + queries.
% 76-year-old man: months of progressive weight loss, fatigue, declining
% functional status; tense large-volume ascites; palpable splenomegaly; no
% alcohol / no known liver disease / no metabolic-or-drug liver injury;
% cholestatic-predominant chemistry (ALP markedly elevated 540, AST 152,
% ALT 68, bilirubin 3.1); anemia + thrombocytopenia; high-SAAG (>1.1)
% portal-hypertensive ascites with cytology negative for malignancy; full
% viral / metabolic / autoimmune / zoonotic work-up negative; imaging away
% from cirrhosis and from venous-outflow obstruction; no dominant hepatic
% mass but splenic lesions; PET-CT diffuse FDG uptake in liver, spleen, and
% marrow; marrow aspirate + peripheral flow both unrevealing.
% Numeric/unit term-args normalized to qualitative atoms for the IDENT grammar.

